What is Seat Pneumatic Lumbar Support?
Seat pneumatic lumbar support refers to an air‑bladder‑based comfort system that is built into vehicle seating structures. By inflating or deflating a sealed bladder under electronic or manual control, the system dynamically adjusts lumbar pressure, improves spinal alignment, reduces driver fatigue on long journeys and enhances overall occupant posture. Modern implementations combine the bladder with sensors, real‑time control units and software algorithms that auto‑tune pressure based on occupant movement, heart‑rate cues or seat‑occupancy data.
